In article <2db67s$1lh@mercury.dur.ac.uk>, Alexis Manning <Alexis.Manning@durham.ac.uk> writes:
>This is probably a stupid question, but how often are new versions of 
>NetHack released, and do the Dev Team actually solicit suggestions for 
>the updates or come up with them off their own bat?
>
>If they are released regularly, when's the next version (Whatever it's 
>going to be called) going to be released?

They are released at highly variable intervals.  I don't think the 
Dev team really solicits suggestions, but they do read this news group.

(I can still recall a discussion about polypiling in 3.0j.  Someone
suggested that if you can get killed by a system shock, maybe your
shoes should have to roll for polymorph survival too.  I replied that
maybe we should allow unrestricted polypiling, but make it riskier...
add a chance of bugs on the floor being turned into demons or something.
Sure enough in 3.1 the items may disappear or turn into golems.  I got
killed by an iron golem while polypiling the other day.  Serves me right,
I should've kept my big mouth shut.  So they're listening...)
